779
00:30:32,680 --> 00:30:41,320
So I showed with the theoretical guarantee that in order to recover on a flat rate, you only need to look into one step of the future.

780
00:30:41,800 --> 00:30:43,820
There is no need to look into more steps.

781
00:30:44,160 --> 00:30:45,180
And I did guarantee.

782
00:30:45,180 --> 00:30:52,360
So basically, I showed that with the optimization problem that I wrote, there is a guarantee.

783
00:30:52,720 --> 00:31:00,660
That if the robot can recover with taking infinite step, my program will find infinite steps to recover from that.

784
